# studies-archive-tracking-diagnostics-2026-07

> The July 2026 diagnosis of the reconstruction's energy and longitudinal-vertex bias, and the
> charge-versus-time tension behind it. Every switch below was a diagnostic of one question; none is
> set by any config in the tree, on any branch, or by any of the 324 published configs and HDF5
> provenance records under `LUCiD_tracking/paper`. What the paper kept from this work is in the
> shipped defaults, not here: the energy taken from the total-charge scale (`energy_from_scale`,
> `energy_scale_mode='nphot'`), the SIREN emitter's importance seed sampling, the single fit from a
> pre-fit margin pick, and `time_weight=0.75` above 1600 MeV.

## The switches, what each was for, and what replaced it

| switch (pipeline config) | added | what it did | today |
|---|---|---|---|
| `fix_energy` | 07-04 | E pinned to truth: no energy scan, E row/column of the step zeroed (`_FixedParamsModel`) | the energy bias it localised is removed by `energy_from_scale` |
| `fix_geometry` | 07-04 | everything but E pinned to truth, one fit from the truth vector (`reconstruct_free_E`) | as above; `_prepare_event(seeds=False)` keeps the data-only preparation the loss-landscape figure needs |
| `e_refit_iters` | 07-04 | a second 1-D Gauss-Newton on `0.5 (ΣQpred(E) − ΣQobs)²` after the fit | the main fit takes energy from the total charge |
| `force_seed` | 07-04 | bypass the pre-fit pick | — |
| `siren_threshold` | 07-04 | monkeypatched `lucid.simulation.simulator.unpack_siren_params` to change `ray_sampling.threshold` | inert under importance sampling; the threshold and the uniform seeding mode are removed from `lucid.siren` |
| `multistart` | 07-02 | three full fits, post-fit pick (`fit_track_multistart`, which stays in the library) | off since 07-04: one fit from the pre-fit pick, ~2.2x faster |
| `tts_walk_corr` (`_cond` `n`/`mu`, `_scale`) | 07-08 | shift observed first arrivals by the TTS order-statistic walk `tts·E[min of n]`, by monkeypatching `lucid.fitting.recon.first_arrival_window_nll` | never in a committed config; no result recorded |
| `pseudodata` | 07-08 | replace the PhotonSim photons with photons sampled from the SIREN emitter (closure data) | see below |
| `gn.time_soft_mode='project'` | 07-08 | project the time term off the vertex–t0 soft mode `(0.285 m along track, +1 ns)`; became `lucid.fitting.ProjectedReconProblem` | the paper balances charge and time with `time_weight` instead |
| `seed_event` | 07-02 | seed-only scoring (no fit) for the seed study | the fused-seed validation it produced is quoted in `reconstruct`'s docstring |

## What is in this tarball

| path | from | what it is |
|---|---|---|
| `analysis/tracking/configs/nominal/` | `58af5a4c` | the 11 campaign configs: nominal, `_ad`, `_fixE`, `_freeE`, `thr0005`/`thr001` scans at 100k–1M rays |
| `analysis/tracking/{charge_ratio,eterm_scan,grad_vs_fd,grad_vs_fd_qnll,grad_vs_fd_qtot,siren_emission_check}.py` | `58af5a4c` | truth-charge ratio; charge/time loss terms vs E; AD-vs-FD gradient zeros in E (localised the +90 MeV bias to the detached time NLL and the per-PMT assignment gradients); emitter vs data emission profiles |
| `analysis/tracking/{loss_split,score_decomp,term_split_scan,profile_sweep,residual_maps,measure_raygaps}.py` | `252f89b8` | charge and time NLL at the fit; per-term score and curvature at truth, the soft-mode projection and the zero-bias `time_weight`; longitudinal term tension; emission calibration vs E; residual maps at truth; the photon-level quantities the ray model does not simulate |
| `analysis/tracking/pipeline.py` | `252f89b8` | the pipeline the scripts import, with every switch |
| `analysis/paper/utils/pipeline.py` | `462a09fd` | the same pipeline as it last stood in `analysis/paper`, on the shared fitting loop |
| `lucid/fitting/recon.py`, `tests/test_recon_projected_problem.py` | `462a09fd` | `ProjectedReconProblem` and its gate against the hand-written projected loop |

## Known defects, read before running anything

1. **Two switches patch library modules for the whole process.** `tts_walk_corr` replaces
   `lucid.fitting.recon.first_arrival_window_nll` and marks it `_fawn_wrapped`, so it stays wrapped
   for every later `TrackingPipeline` in the process, including ones that did not ask for it;
   `siren_threshold` replaces `lucid.simulation.simulator.unpack_siren_params` the same way. In a
   loop over configs (`run_local`), one config contaminates the rest.
2. **`siren_threshold` measured nothing after 2026-07-03.** The threshold is read only by
   `seed_mode='uniform'`; the default became `'importance'` that day, and the `thr*` configs do not
   set the mode back.
3. **The configs run on 2026-07 defaults**, not the published recipe: they override `gn` with
   `fisher_mode='ad', lr=1.0` and inherit everything else from the pipeline of that date (tts and
   sigma 2.5, 4 keys, 250 iterations, no charge-resolution model). Their numbers are not paper numbers.
4. **The scripts import `analysis.tracking`**, which no longer exists; run them against `252f89b8`.

## `pseudodata` and the open energy-bias question

The closure switch was used again in 2026-09, on branch `worktree-restructure-paper-analysis`
(`docs/internal/restructure/OPEN_ITEMS.md` §10 and its uncommitted `evidence/cause/`), to split the
fitted-energy bias into a Monte-Carlo (Jensen) term, an emitter term and a remainder. At 1500 MeV,
100 events: total −7.46 ± 2.90 MeV; 250k → 1M rays +1.40 ± 0.23; closure − real +4.83 ± 3.28
(z 1.5, unresolved); remainder with the emitter matched and 4x the rays −5.73 ± 2.80, attributed to
the detection path. The 1000 MeV arms are incomplete. That material is not in this asset.

If the question is reopened, closure data belongs in the library as a capability (simulate an
event from the model's own emitter, the reconstruction analogue of `lucid.fitting.closure_data`),
used by any application, not as a branch inside one application's pipeline.
